<figure id="algorithm2" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span>Grid-based Action Quantization (cell <math id="algorithm2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\to" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\to</annotation></semantics></math> code)</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm2.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>Dim <math id="algorithm2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, requested codes <math id="algorithm2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\rm req}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>req</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\rm req}</annotation></semantics></math>, bins <math id="algorithm2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{\rm req}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>req</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{\rm req}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm2.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span><math id="algorithm2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\{0,\dots,N{-}1\}^{b^{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\{0,\dots,N{-}1\}^{b^{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\leftarrow\min\!\big\{8,\,\max\!\{2,\,\lfloor N_{\rm req}^{1/D}\rfloor\}\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.653em;" width="1.653em"><mi>min</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>8</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.808em;" width="1.808em"><mi>max</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>req</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\leftarrow\min\!\big\{8,\,\max\!\{2,\,\lfloor N_{\rm req}^{1/D}\rfloor\}\big\}</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="algorithm2.4.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.3.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{D}&gt;N_{\rm req}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>req</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{D}&gt;N_{\rm req}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.4.3.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> <math id="algorithm2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b&gt;2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b&gt;2</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\leftarrow b-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\leftarrow b-1</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.5.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\geq 6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\geq 6</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.4.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">and</span> <math id="algorithm2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{D}&gt;N_{\rm req}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>req</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{D}&gt;N_{\rm req}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leftarrow\min(b^{D},128)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>128</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leftarrow\min(b^{D},128)</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">6</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leftarrow N_{\rm req}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>req</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leftarrow N_{\rm req}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.9.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.4.9.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N-1</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8</span></span>
            Let <math id="algorithm2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}\in\{0,\dots,b-1\}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}\in\{0,\dots,b-1\}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be the base-<math id="algorithm2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> digits of <math id="algorithm2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">9</span></span>
            Set code <math id="algorithm2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}\in[-1,1]^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}\in[-1,1]^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="algorithm2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}[d]\leftarrow\tfrac{2\,g_{i}[d]}{b-1}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}[d]\leftarrow\tfrac{2\,g_{i}[d]}{b-1}-1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="algorithm2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1..D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1..D</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">10</span></span>
            Allocate <math id="algorithm2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="algorithm2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">11</span></span>
            <span id="algorithm2.4.13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <em id="algorithm2.4.13.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">cells <math id="algorithm2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.4.13.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_upright">to</span> <math id="algorithm2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{D}{-}1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mi>D</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{D}{-}1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algorithm2.4.13.3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">in batches</span></em> <span id="algorithm2.4.13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.14.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">12</span></span>
            Map <math id="algorithm2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="algorithm2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> (base-<math id="algorithm2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>) and <math id="algorithm2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{\ell}[d]\leftarrow\tfrac{2\,g_{\ell}[d]}{b-1}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{\ell}[d]\leftarrow\tfrac{2\,g_{\ell}[d]}{b-1}-1</annotation></semantics></math>;
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> 
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">13</span></span>
            <math id="algorithm2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T[\ell]\leftarrow\argmin_{i\in\{0,\dots,N-1\}}\|a_{\ell}-c_{i}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>min</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T[\ell]\leftarrow\argmin_{i\in\{0,\dots,N-1\}}\|a_{\ell}-c_{i}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>   <span id="algorithm2.4.15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">// </span><span id="algorithm2.4.15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">vectorized on GPU</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm2.4.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">14</span></span>
            Cache <math id="algorithm2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> under key <math id="algorithm2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(D,b,N,\text{env})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>env</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(D,b,N,\text{env})</annotation></semantics></math> and return
</div>
<div id="algorithm2.4.17" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Injecting Attractions into Attention</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times H\times S\times S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times H\times S\times S}</annotation></semantics></math> denote pre-softmax attention logits over tokenized returns, states, and actions. Let <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{act}}\subset\{1,\ldots,S\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>act</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{act}}\subset\{1,\ldots,S\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the action-token column indices and let <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(i)</annotation></semantics></math> be the timestep associated with action column <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. From (<a href="#S4.E9" title="In 4.1 Experience–Weighted Attraction (EWA) for Decision Transformers ‣ 4 Method ‣ Mental Accounts for Actions: EWA-Inspired Attention in Decision Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), define the per-batch, per-head <em id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">attraction bias</em> as</p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{n,h,:,i}\;=\;\begin{cases}\beta\,A_{j_{t(i)}}(t(i))\,\mathbf{1}_{S},&amp;i\in\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{act}},\\[3.0pt]
\mathbf{0}_{S},&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}\qquad\tilde{W}\;=\;W\;+\;B," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mo rspace="0em">:</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mi>act</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext>otherwise</mtext><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>W</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0.502em" rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{n,h,:,i}\;=\;\begin{cases}\beta\,A_{j_{t(i)}}(t(i))\,\mathbf{1}_{S},&amp;i\in\mathcal{I}_{\mathrm{act}},\\[3.0pt]
\mathbf{0}_{S},&amp;\text{otherwise},\end{cases}\qquad\tilde{W}\;=\;W\;+\;B,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> is a length-<math id="S4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> all-ones vector (broadcast along rows) and <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> is a small scalar (or per-head scale; see ablations). We then apply the usual causal/padding masks and softmax. Intuitively, <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\,A_{j_{t(i)}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\,A_{j_{t(i)}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a column-bias that increases (decreases) attention mass toward action tokens with stronger (weaker) accumulated attraction—an explicit, recency-weighted memory of success and failure.<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
            We keep the attention architecture unchanged: the bias is additive, applied before masking/softmax.</span></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Controlled attention drift under a bounded bias)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\mathrm{softmax}(z)\in\Delta^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\mathrm{softmax}(z)\in\Delta^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\mathrm{softmax}(z+b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\mathrm{softmax}(z+b)</annotation></semantics></math> for any bias <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|b\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|b\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the total variation distance satisfies</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\;\leq\;\tanh(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\;\leq\;\tanh(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof sketch.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The likelihood ratio <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}/p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}/p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded in <math id="S4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[e^{-2\varepsilon},e^{2\varepsilon}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[e^{-2\varepsilon},e^{2\varepsilon}]</annotation></semantics></math>, which implies
<math id="S4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\tanh(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\leq\tanh(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Full details are in Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Proof of Lemma ‣ Appendix A Proofs of Theoretical Results ‣ Mental Accounts for Actions: EWA-Inspired Attention in Decision Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Intuitively, perturbing logits by at most <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> constrains each attention probability’s multiplicative change to <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[e^{-2\varepsilon},e^{2\varepsilon}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[e^{-2\varepsilon},e^{2\varepsilon}]</annotation></semantics></math>; the worst case occurs when some entries get the full boost and others the full suppression, yielding the <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> bound. For small <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(\varepsilon)\!\approx\!\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≈</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(\varepsilon)\!\approx\!\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, so clipping <math id="S4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\beta A\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\beta A\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> provides a simple, interpretable cap on attention drift.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Setup</h3>

<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Environments.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate on two D4RL continuous-control benchmarks: <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hopper-medium-v2</span> (action dim. <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>) and <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">walker2d-medium-replay-v2</span> (<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d{=}6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d{=}6</annotation></semantics></math>). Datasets contain suboptimal offline trajectories; we fine-tune online following the standard offline-to-online protocol.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Baselines.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EWA–VQ–ODT</span> to the <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Online Decision Transformer (ODT)</span>. Architectures (backbone width/depth), tokenization, context length, optimizer, and training schedules are matched.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training configuration.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless noted: <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> online iterations with evaluation every two iterations; batch size <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math>; context length <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K{=}20,5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K{=}20,5</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hopper-medium-v2</span> and <span id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">walker2d-medium-replay-v2</span>, respectively; Adam (<math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{lr}{=}10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>lr</mtext><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{lr}{=}10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>) with linear warmup; <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> evaluation episodes per checkpoint; <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> random seeds.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">EWA–VQ–ODT hyperparameters.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attention bias scale <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta{=}0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta{=}0.05</annotation></semantics></math>; decay <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi{=}0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi{=}0.05</annotation></semantics></math>; chosen weight <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta{=}0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta{=}0.8</annotation></semantics></math>; codebook size <math id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M{=}27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M{=}27</annotation></semantics></math>; grid bins chosen adaptively per dimension.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation protocol.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At each checkpoint we compute per-seed metrics; we then average across seeds at each step, and finally average those per-step means across all training steps to obtain a single scalar per (environment, algorithm, metric). Improvements are reported as relative change vs. ODT.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Metrics</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We follow the ODT codebase and report seven metrics:</p>
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">evaluation/return_mean_gm</span>: geometric mean of evaluation returns</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">evaluation/return_std_gm</span>: variability of evaluation returns</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">evaluation/return_vs_samples</span>: return as a function of consumed environment steps</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">evaluation/length_mean_gm</span>: geometric mean of evaluation episode lengths</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">evaluation/length_std_gm</span>: variability of episode lengths</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">aug_traj/return</span>: return of trajectories generated during fine-tuning</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">aug_traj/length</span>: length of trajectories generated during fine-tuning</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Main Results</h3>

<figure id="S5.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2509.15498v1/images/222401_evaluation_combined.png" id="S5.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:438/271;" width="438" height="271" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><img src="2509.15498v1/images/230225_evaluation_combined.png" id="S5.F2.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:438/271;" width="438" height="271" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F2.11" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 2</span>: </span><span id="S5.F2.12" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Evaluation curves.
Top: <span id="S5.F2.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">walker2d-medium-replay-v2</span>, where EWA–VQ–ODT substantially improves <em id="S5.F2.12.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Return Mean Gm</em>, <em id="S5.F2.12.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Length Mean Gm</em>, and <em id="S5.F2.12.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Return vs Samples</em>, with higher mid-training variance reflecting volatility in the higher-dimensional action space.
Bottom: <span id="S5.F2.12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hopper-medium-v2</span>, where gains are modest but consistent: EWA–VQ–ODT raises <em id="S5.F2.12.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Return Mean Gm</em>, <em id="S5.F2.12.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Length Mean Gm</em>, and <em id="S5.F2.12.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Return vs Samples</em>, while reducing variance for more stable policies.
Shaded bands show <math id="S5.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 1</annotation></semantics></math> geometric std across seeds.</span></figcaption>
