<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs of Theoretical Results</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Closed form, boundedness, steady state). ‣ Why the simplified form? ‣ 4.1 Experience–Weighted Attraction (EWA) for Decision Transformers ‣ 4 Method ‣ Mental Accounts for Actions: EWA-Inspired Attention in Decision Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 4.1 (Closed form, boundedness, steady state). ‣ Why the simplified form? ‣ 4.1 Experience–Weighted Attraction (EWA) for Decision Transformers ‣ 4 Method ‣ Mental Accounts for Actions: EWA-Inspired Attention in Decision Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></span> [Closed form, boundedness, steady state]</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let the per-code attraction follow the simplified EWA update</p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{\ell}(t)=(1-\phi)A_{\ell}(t-1)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\},\quad\phi\in(0,1),\quad|\tilde{r}_{t}|\leq R." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}(t)=(1-\phi)A_{\ell}(t-1)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\},\quad\phi\in(0,1),\quad|\tilde{r}_{t}|\leq R.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Then <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a closed form, is uniformly bounded by
<math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta R/\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta R/\phi</annotation></semantics></math>, and under stationarity satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}\,\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]\;=\;\frac{\delta\,p_{\ell}\,\mu_{\ell}}{\phi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}\,\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]\;=\;\frac{\delta\,p_{\ell}\,\mu_{\ell}}{\phi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">As described in the main text, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>: the “attraction” (memory) for action code <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> after step <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.
Update rule (simplified EWA) is:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{\ell}(t)=(1-\phi)\,A_{\ell}(t-1)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}(t)=(1-\phi)\,A_{\ell}(t-1)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\phi&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\phi&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> is the decay rate, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> scales new rewards, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{r}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{r}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded with <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tilde{r}_{t}|\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tilde{r}_{t}|\leq R</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the code chosen at time <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator of choosing <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Every step shrinks all memories by <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\phi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\phi)</annotation></semantics></math> and adds <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\tilde{r}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\tilde{r}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> only to the chosen code’s memory.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Step 1: Closed form</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unrolling the recursion gives:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex7X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle A_{\ell}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle A_{\ell}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\phi)A_{\ell}(t-1)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\phi)A_{\ell}(t-1)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\phi)\Big[(1-\phi)A_{\ell}(t-2)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t-1}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t-1}\}\Big]+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\phi)\Big[(1-\phi)A_{\ell}(t-2)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t-1}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t-1}\}\Big]+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\phi)^{2}A_{\ell}(t-2)+(1-\phi)\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t-1}\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t-1}\}+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\phi)^{2}A_{\ell}(t-2)+(1-\phi)\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t-1}\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t-1}\}+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\vdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">⋮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\vdots</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\phi)^{t}A_{\ell}(0)+\delta\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{\,t-\tau}\,\tilde{r}_{\tau}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\phi)^{t}A_{\ell}(0)+\delta\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{\,t-\tau}\,\tilde{r}_{\tau}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SSx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">It demonstrates that <math id="A1.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> is a geometrically decayed sum of past realized rewards for code <math id="A1.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Step 2: Uniform boundedness</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We start from the unrolled form, which is already established:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{\ell}(t)\;=\;(1-\phi)^{t}A_{\ell}(0)\;+\;\delta\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\,\tilde{r}_{\tau}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>δ</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}(t)\;=\;(1-\phi)^{t}A_{\ell}(0)\;+\;\delta\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\,\tilde{r}_{\tau}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, apply the triangle inequality and absolute values to separate the two terms:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;|(1-\phi)^{t}A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta\left|\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\,\tilde{r}_{\tau}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}\right|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.169em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.058em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;|(1-\phi)^{t}A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta\left|\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\,\tilde{r}_{\tau}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}\right|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SSx2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This step follows because <math id="A1.SSx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|x+y|\leq|x|+|y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|x+y|\leq|x|+|y|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, pull the absolute value inside the sum:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\,|\tilde{r}_{\tau}|\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.169em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.058em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>δ</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\,|\tilde{r}_{\tau}|\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SSx2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This uses the fact that <math id="A1.SSx2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big|\sum u_{\tau}\big|\leq\sum|u_{\tau}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big|\sum u_{\tau}\big|\leq\sum|u_{\tau}|</annotation></semantics></math>. Also, <math id="A1.SSx2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}|=(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}|=(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A1.SSx2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\phi)\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\phi)\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SSx2.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}|=\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">=</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}|=\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}</annotation></semantics></math> since the indicator is always 0 or 1.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Now, apply the reward bound and indicator bound. Since <math id="A1.SSx2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tilde{r}_{\tau}|\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tilde{r}_{\tau}|\leq R</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SSx2.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, each term can be bounded as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\,R\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta R\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.169em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.058em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>δ</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mi>R</mi><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.058em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>R</mi><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\,R\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{\tau}\}\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta R\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Reindex the geometric sum by setting <math id="A1.SSx2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=t-\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=t-\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. As <math id="A1.SSx2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> goes from <math id="A1.SSx2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SSx2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SSx2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> goes from <math id="A1.SSx2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t-1</annotation></semantics></math> down to <math id="A1.SSx2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\;=\;\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}(1-\phi)^{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\tau=1}^{t}(1-\phi)^{t-\tau}\;=\;\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}(1-\phi)^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SSx2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">Hence</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta R\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}(1-\phi)^{k}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\delta R\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}(1-\phi)^{k}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, upper-bound the finite geometric series by the infinite one:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}(1-\phi)^{k}\;\leq\;\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\phi)^{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{\phi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">≤</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ϕ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k=0}^{t-1}(1-\phi)^{k}\;\leq\;\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}(1-\phi)^{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{\phi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SSx2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">This holds because <math id="A1.SSx2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;1-\phi&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;1-\phi&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and all terms are nonnegative, so extending the sum can only increase it. Therefore</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\frac{\delta R}{\phi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\frac{\delta R}{\phi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">In summary, the general uniform bound, without assuming a particular initialization, is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\frac{\delta R}{\phi}\;\leq\;|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\frac{\delta R}{\phi}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\frac{\delta R}{\phi}\;\leq\;|A_{\ell}(0)|\;+\;\frac{\delta R}{\phi},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SSx2.p7.2" class="ltx_p">since <math id="A1.SSx2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\phi)^{t}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\phi)^{t}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. If we initialize <math id="A1.SSx2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> as in Algorithm 1, the bound simplifies to</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;\frac{\delta R}{\phi}\qquad\text{for all }t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|A_{\ell}(t)|\;\leq\;\frac{\delta R}{\phi}\qquad\text{for all }t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SSx2.p7.3" class="ltx_p">Even if <math id="A1.SSx2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{\ell}(0)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}(0)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, the extra term <math id="A1.SSx2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\phi)^{t}|A_{\ell}(0)|</annotation></semantics></math> decays to zero, so the bound tightens to <math id="A1.SSx2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta R/\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta R/\phi</annotation></semantics></math> over time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Step 3: Steady state (long-run expectation)</h3>

<div id="A1.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin again from the one-step update:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="A_{\ell}(t)=(1-\phi)A_{\ell}(t-1)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{\ell}(t)=(1-\phi)A_{\ell}(t-1)+\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Taking expectations on both sides and applying linearity gives</p>
<table id="A1.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]=(1-\phi)\,\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t-1)]+\delta\,\mathbb{E}\big[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]=(1-\phi)\,\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t-1)]+\delta\,\mathbb{E}\big[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Now compute <math id="A1.SSx3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}]</annotation></semantics></math> by conditioning on <math id="A1.SSx3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}]=\mathbb{E}\big[\;\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}\mid j_{t}]\;\big]=\mathbb{E}\big[\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}\,\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\mid j_{t}]\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">[</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mn>𝟏</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}]=\mathbb{E}\big[\;\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}\mid j_{t}]\;\big]=\mathbb{E}\big[\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}\,\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\mid j_{t}]\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By the definitions under stationarity, let <math id="A1.SSx3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\ell}=\Pr(j_{t}=\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\ell}=\Pr(j_{t}=\ell)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SSx3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\ell}=\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\mid j_{t}=\ell]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\ell}=\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\mid j_{t}=\ell]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}]=\sum_{j}\Pr(j_{t}=j)\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j\}\,\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\mid j_{t}=j]=p_{\ell}\mu_{\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></munder><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j_{t}\}]=\sum_{j}\Pr(j_{t}=j)\,\mathbf{1}\{\ell=j\}\,\mathbb{E}[\tilde{r}_{t}\mid j_{t}=j]=p_{\ell}\mu_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting back, the recursion for expectations becomes</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]=(1-\phi)\,\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t-1)]\;+\;\delta\,p_{\ell}\,\mu_{\ell}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]=(1-\phi)\,\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t-1)]\;+\;\delta\,p_{\ell}\,\mu_{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="A1.SSx3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}:=\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}:=\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SSx3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha:=1-\phi\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha:=1-\phi\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.SSx3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c:=\delta\,p_{\ell}\,\mu_{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c:=\delta\,p_{\ell}\,\mu_{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, the recursion is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}=\alpha\,y_{t-1}+c." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}=\alpha\,y_{t-1}+c.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The general solution to this linear difference equation is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}=\alpha^{t}y_{0}+\frac{c}{1-\alpha}\bigl(1-\alpha^{t}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}=\alpha^{t}y_{0}+\frac{c}{1-\alpha}\bigl(1-\alpha^{t}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A1.SSx3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1-\phi\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1-\phi\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A1.SSx3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha^{t}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mi>t</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha^{t}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SSx3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}\,\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]\;=\;\frac{c}{1-\alpha}=\frac{\delta\,p_{\ell}\,\mu_{\ell}}{\phi}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}\,\mathbb{E}[A_{\ell}(t)]\;=\;\frac{c}{1-\alpha}=\frac{\delta\,p_{\ell}\,\mu_{\ell}}{\phi}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Equivalently, we can check the fixed point directly: setting <math id="A1.SSx3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}=y_{t-1}=y_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}=y_{t-1}=y_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> in the recursion yields</p>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\star}=\alpha y_{\star}+c," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\star}=\alpha y_{\star}+c,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SSx3.p9.2" class="ltx_p">whose solution is <math id="A1.SSx3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\star}=\tfrac{c}{1-\alpha}=\tfrac{\delta p_{\ell}\mu_{\ell}}{\phi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msub></mrow><mi>ϕ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\star}=\tfrac{c}{1-\alpha}=\tfrac{\delta p_{\ell}\mu_{\ell}}{\phi}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SSx3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\alpha|&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\alpha|&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the recursion is a contraction and converges to this unique fixed point.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SSx3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SSx3.p10.1" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Ex3" title="Lemma 4.2 (Controlled attention drift under a bounded bias). ‣ 4.3 Injecting Attractions into Attention ‣ 4 Method ‣ Mental Accounts for Actions: EWA-Inspired Attention in Decision Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma <a href="#S4.Ex3" title="Lemma 4.2 (Controlled attention drift under a bounded bias). ‣ 4.3 Injecting Attractions into Attention ‣ 4 Method ‣ Mental Accounts for Actions: EWA-Inspired Attention in Decision Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a></span>[Controlled attention drift under a bounded bias]</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\mathrm{softmax}(z)\in\Delta^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\mathrm{softmax}(z)\in\Delta^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\mathrm{softmax}(z+b)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\mathrm{softmax}(z+b)</annotation></semantics></math> for any bias <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|b\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|b\|_{\infty}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the total variation distance satisfies</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\;\leq\;\tanh(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}\;\leq\;\tanh(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We begin by recalling definitions. The softmax distribution is given by <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}}}{\sum_{j}e^{z_{j}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}}}{\sum_{j}e^{z_{j}}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}+b_{i}}}{\sum_{j}e^{z_{j}+b_{j}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub></mstyle><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}+b_{i}}}{\sum_{j}e^{z_{j}+b_{j}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The total variation (TV) distance is <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i}|q_{i}-p_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\tfrac{1}{2}\sum_{i}|q_{i}-p_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>. This measures the discrepancy between two probability distributions, taking values in <math id="A1.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">To analyze this bound, we first express <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>. Multiplying and dividing by <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k}e^{z_{k}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k}e^{z_{k}}</annotation></semantics></math>, one obtains</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}+b_{i}}}{\sum_{j}e^{z_{j}+b_{j}}}=\frac{e^{b_{i}}}{\sum_{j}p_{j}e^{b_{j}}}\,p_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\frac{e^{z_{i}+b_{i}}}{\sum_{j}e^{z_{j}+b_{j}}}=\frac{e^{b_{i}}}{\sum_{j}p_{j}e^{b_{j}}}\,p_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Letting <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\sum_{j}p_{j}e^{b_{j}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\sum_{j}p_{j}e^{b_{j}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}=e^{b_{i}}/Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}=e^{b_{i}}/Z</annotation></semantics></math>, this simplifies to <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\lambda_{i}p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\lambda_{i}p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{i}\lambda_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{i}\lambda_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, so the <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-weighted average of the reweighting factors <math id="A1.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is exactly one.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we bound the reweighting factors. Since <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{i}\in[-\varepsilon,\varepsilon]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{i}\in[-\varepsilon,\varepsilon]</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows that <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{b_{i}}\in[e^{-\varepsilon},e^{\varepsilon}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{b_{i}}\in[e^{-\varepsilon},e^{\varepsilon}]</annotation></semantics></math>. The denominator <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> is a convex combination of such terms, so <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in[e^{-\varepsilon},e^{\varepsilon}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in[e^{-\varepsilon},e^{\varepsilon}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}=\frac{e^{b_{i}}}{Z}\in\left[\frac{e^{-\varepsilon}}{e^{\varepsilon}},\frac{e^{\varepsilon}}{e^{-\varepsilon}}\right]=[e^{-2\varepsilon},e^{2\varepsilon}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>ε</mi></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}=\frac{e^{b_{i}}}{Z}\in\left[\frac{e^{-\varepsilon}}{e^{\varepsilon}},\frac{e^{\varepsilon}}{e^{-\varepsilon}}\right]=[e^{-2\varepsilon},e^{2\varepsilon}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">so each likelihood ratio <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}/p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}/p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded between <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=e^{-2\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=e^{-2\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=e^{2\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=e^{2\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ab=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ab=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now we express the TV distance in terms of these reweighting factors:</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i}|q_{i}-p_{i}|=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i}p_{i}\,|\lambda_{i}-1|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i}|q_{i}-p_{i}|=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{i}p_{i}\,|\lambda_{i}-1|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Partitioning indices into <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{i:\lambda_{i}\geq 1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{i:\lambda_{i}\geq 1\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, and using the fact that <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{i}\lambda_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{i}\lambda_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> implies <math id="A1.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{i}(\lambda_{i}-1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{i}(\lambda_{i}-1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we deduce that</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\sum_{i\in S}p_{i}(\lambda_{i}-1)=\sum_{i\in S^{c}}p_{i}(1-\lambda_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mi>c</mi></msup></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\sum_{i\in S}p_{i}(\lambda_{i}-1)=\sum_{i\in S^{c}}p_{i}(1-\lambda_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus TV reduces to the total “mass shifted upwards” (or downwards), and both are equal.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">To maximize this deviation under the constraints <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\in[a,b]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\in[a,b]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{i}\lambda_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{i}\lambda_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, one only needs to consider extreme points where each <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> equals either <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>a</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math>. The worst case occurs with a two-point mixture: set <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=b</annotation></semantics></math> on some fraction <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> of the <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-mass and <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=a</annotation></semantics></math> on the rest. Enforcing <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}p_{i}\lambda_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}p_{i}\lambda_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> yields <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1=sb+(1-s)a" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1=sb+(1-s)a</annotation></semantics></math>, hence <math id="A1.SS2.p7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=\frac{1-a}{b-a}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=\frac{1-a}{b-a}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting into the expression for TV gives</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\frac{1}{2}\big(s(b-1)+(1-s)(1-a)\big)=\frac{(1-a)(b-1)}{b-a}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\frac{1}{2}\big(s(b-1)+(1-s)(1-a)\big)=\frac{(1-a)(b-1)}{b-a}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, substituting <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=e^{-2\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=e^{-2\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b=e^{2\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b=e^{2\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\frac{b-1}{b+1}=\frac{e^{2\varepsilon}-1}{e^{2\varepsilon}+1}=\tanh(\varepsilon)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi>TV</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|q-p\|_{\mathrm{TV}}=\frac{b-1}{b+1}=\frac{e^{2\varepsilon}-1}{e^{2\varepsilon}+1}=\tanh(\varepsilon).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">This establishes the desired bound. Intuitively, the perturbation <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> shifts logits by at most <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, so each attention probability can change by a factor in <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[e^{-2\varepsilon},e^{2\varepsilon}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[e^{-2\varepsilon},e^{2\varepsilon}]</annotation></semantics></math>. The worst-case change occurs when some entries receive the full amplification while others receive the full suppression, balanced to maintain normalization. This yields the clean <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(\varepsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(\varepsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> formula. For small <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, the bound behaves linearly, <math id="A1.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tanh(\varepsilon)\approx\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>tanh</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tanh(\varepsilon)\approx\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, so clipping the bias ensures the drift remains small and interpretable.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Hyperparameters for <span id="A2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">EWA–VQ–ODT</span></h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless noted, all runs use the same backbone and optimizer as the ODT baseline. The values below reflect the configurations used in our main experiments.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Core EWA–VQ Settings</h3>

<figure id="A2.SS1.tab1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A2.SS1.tab1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Parameter</span></th>
<th id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Value</span></th>
<th id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Description</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Attraction decay <math id="A2.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="A2.SS1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Per–step global decay: <math id="A2.SS1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\!\leftarrow\!(1-\phi)A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.128em" rspace="0.128em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\!\leftarrow\!(1-\phi)A</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Chosen weight <math id="A2.SS1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.SS1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Additive update for routed code: <math id="A2.SS1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{j_{t}}\!+\!=\!\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mi>j</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mpadded style="width:0.628em;" width="0.628em"><mo lspace="0.072em">+</mo></mpadded></mrow><mo rspace="0.128em">=</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>r</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{j_{t}}\!+\!=\!\delta\,\tilde{r}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Attention bias scale <math id="A2.SS1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.SS1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Scales the attraction bias added to action columns</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Trajectory length (max)</span></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.SS1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">1000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1000</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Max steps processed per trajectory</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">VQ codebook size <math id="A2.SS1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.SS1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">27</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">27</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Number of discrete action surrogates (codes)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Grid bins factor</span></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.SS1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.7.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Adaptive bins per action dim (see below)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Routing</span></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.8.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">direct lookup</span></td>
<td id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><span id="A2.SS1.tab1.1.8.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Grid cell <math id="A2.SS1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!\to\!" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!\to\!</annotation></semantics></math> code index via cached table <math id="A2.SS1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}</annotation></semantics></math></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Codebook/grid construction.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use an axis-aligned grid with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> bins per dimension; for the tasks studied we set <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>. The offline table <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}:\{0,\ldots,B^{d}\!-\!1\}\!\to\!\{1,\ldots,M\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖳</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}:\{0,\ldots,B^{d}\!-\!1\}\!\to\!\{1,\ldots,M\}</annotation></semantics></math> maps each grid cell to its nearest code. The table is cached per <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d,B,M,\text{env})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo>,</mo><mtext>env</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d,B,M,\text{env})</annotation></semantics></math> and reused.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
