<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Grid adaptation rules.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\!\leq\!6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">≤</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\!\leq\!6</annotation></semantics></math>, we use <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> bins/dim. (General logic: <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\!\in\![2,8]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\!\in\![2,8]</annotation></semantics></math> with a cap on <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>—here <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M{=}27" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M{=}27</annotation></semantics></math>; max <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> can be raised up to <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math> if memory allows.) The offline <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{T}</annotation></semantics></math> table is built once (GPU-batched <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) and cached.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation note.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Attractions <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\!\in\!\mathbb{R}^{M}</annotation></semantics></math> are stored on GPU; each step applies one vectorized decay and a single indexed add for the routed code. The attention bias adds <math id="A2.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\,A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\,A</annotation></semantics></math> only to action-token columns prior to masking and softmax.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
